[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2607917463","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101925#issuecomment-2607917463","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101925","id":2607917463,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bcamX","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-22T18:03:30Z","updated_at":"2025-01-22T18:03:30Z","body":"* See #95113.\n\nNot a bug, see the same for typed arrays. But we should document this for dictionaries too, and maybe customize the error message given how often users report this to us.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2607917463/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2608179351","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101925#issuecomment-2608179351","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101925","id":2608179351,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bdaiX","user":{"login":"aaronp64","id":136198872,"node_id":"U_kgDOCB462A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/136198872?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronp64","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-22T20:16:01Z","updated_at":"2025-01-22T20:16:01Z","body":"I think the `Array` case might be different - that looks like trying to treat an array of a subtype as an array of the base type.  This looks more like adding a subtype object to a collection of the base type, which works for `Array`.  Using a modified version of the MRP code from this issue:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar thing := Thing.new()\n\tvar subthing := SubThing.new()\n\t\n\tvar array : Array[Thing] = []\n\tarray.push_back(subthing) # works ok\n\t\n\tvar dictionary : Dictionary[Thing, Thing] = {}\n\tdictionary[thing] = subthing # works ok - subtype objects can be used as values\n\tdictionary[subthing] = thing # parser error - subtype objects cannot be used as keys\n\t\n\tvar node2d := Node2D.new()\n\tvar node3d := Node3D.new()\n\tvar dictionary2 : Dictionary[Node, Node] = {}\n\tdictionary2[node2d] = node3d # works ok\n\nclass Thing:\n\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t\tpass\n\t\t\nclass SubThing:\n\textends Thing\n\t\n\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t\tpass\n\n```\n\nThis seems to only apply to script subclasses used as keys - values and built in subclasses seem to work ok","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2608179351/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2609713326","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101925#issuecomment-2609713326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101925","id":2609713326,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bjRCu","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-23T12:42:01Z","updated_at":"2025-01-23T12:42:01Z","body":"For me that's definitely a bug. Note it works fine using `set` method instead of `operator []` (so that's a possible workaround for now):\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar thing := Thing.new()\n\tvar subthing := SubThing.new()\n\t\n\tvar dictionary : Dictionary[Thing, Thing] = {}\n\tdictionary[thing] = subthing # works ok - subtype objects can be used as values\n\tdictionary.set(subthing, thing) # works ok - subtype objects can be used as keys, as expected\n\tdictionary[subthing] = thing # Parser Error: Invalid index type \"SubThing\" for a base of type \"Dictionary[Thing, Thing]\".\n\n\nclass Thing:\n\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t\tpass\n\t\t\nclass SubThing:\n\textends Thing\n\t\n\tfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t\tpass\n```\n\nSeems related to #96797, cc @Repiteo.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2609713326/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614334766","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101925#issuecomment-2614334766","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101925","id":2614334766,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b05Uu","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-26T11:29:20Z","updated_at":"2025-01-26T11:29:20Z","body":"So for the example from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101925#issuecomment-2609713326 for `dictionary[subthing] = thing` this returns `true` and hence leads to error:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b15b24b087e792335d919fd83055f50f276fbe22/modules/gdscript/gdscript_analyzer.cpp#L4930\n\nAFAICT both `key_type` and `index_type` seem to be `GDScriptParser::DataType`s correctly referring to the inner classes. However, within `GDScriptParser::DataType::can_reference` the  obtained `Script`s (both `if`s are entered):\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b15b24b087e792335d919fd83055f50f276fbe22/modules/gdscript/gdscript_parser.cpp#L5343-L5357\nhave both `GDScript._base` being `null`, which results in `script_other->inherits_script(script)` returning `false`:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b15b24b087e792335d919fd83055f50f276fbe22/modules/gdscript/gdscript_parser.cpp#L5363-L5364\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/b15b24b087e792335d919fd83055f50f276fbe22/modules/gdscript/gdscript.cpp#L1202-L1218","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2614334766/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2621382237","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101925#issuecomment-2621382237","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101925","id":2621382237,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cPx5d","user":{"login":"SeremTitus","id":58259212,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MjU5MjEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58259212?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeremTitus","html_url":"https://github.com/SeremTitus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeremTitus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeremTitus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeremTitus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeremTitus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeremTitus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeremTitus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeremTitus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeremTitus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeremTitus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-29T11:27:17Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T07:00:44Z","body":"> * See [Godot is not checking the subtypes in typed arrays #95113](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/95113).\n> \n> Not a bug, see the same for typed arrays. But we should document this for dictionaries too, and maybe customize the error message given how often users report this to us.\n\n@dalexeev is there a technical limitation for this, since  in `core\\variant\\container_type_validate.h:146`\n```cpp\nERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(!other_script->inherits_script(script), false, vformat(\"Attempted to %s an object into a %s, that does not inherit from '%s'.\", String(p_operation), String(where), String(script->get_class_name())));\n```\nalso `core\\variant\\container_type_validate.h:68`  . Uses inherits_script method to determine if typed array or dictionary can be assigned that a particular object.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2621382237/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4494109766","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101925#issuecomment-4494109766","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101925","id":4494109766,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABC96sRg","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T03:02:23Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T03:02:23Z","body":"This is definitely a bug, and not a duplicate of the `Array` covariance issue that Dal originally linked. This isn't something to do with the type of the `Dictionary` itself, but an issue with how it validates parameters in the `[]` operator compared to `has` / `get` / `set` / etc.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4494109766/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]